# 🧠 Intelligent Recommendation System for E-Learning Platforms

An AI-powered personal career & learning mentor built with **Streamlit** and **Google Gemini**. Unlike generic e-learning platforms, this system personalizes everything — skill-gap analysis, a week-by-week roadmap, trusted course recommendations, quizzes, and a 24/7 doubt-solving chatbot — based on each student's own background and career goal.

## ✨ Features
- Personalized skill-gap analysis (strengths vs. missing skills)
- AI-generated week-by-week learning roadmap
- Smart, fuzzy-matched course recommendation engine
- AI-powered quiz generator with instant scoring
- 24/7 AI doubts chatbot
- Progress tracker with milestone badges (🥉🥈🥇)
- Quiz history dashboard
- One-click PDF export of your roadmap

## 🛠️ Tech Stack
- **Frontend:** Streamlit
- **AI Engine:** Google Gemini API (`google-genai` SDK)
- **Database:** SQLite
- **Other:** Pandas, python-dotenv, fpdf2

## 🚀 Run Locally

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo-name>.git
cd <your-repo-name>

python -m venv env
env\Scripts\activate        # Windows
# source env/bin/activate   # Mac/Linux

pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Create a `.env` file in the project root (copy `.env.example`) and add your key:

```
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_actual_api_key_here
```

Get a free key from [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/apikey).

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

## ☁️ Live Deployment (Streamlit Community Cloud)

1. Push this repo to GitHub (see below).
2. Go to [share.streamlit.io](https://share.streamlit.io) and sign in with GitHub.
3. Click **"New app"** → select this repo → branch `main` → main file `app.py`.
4. Before deploying, click **"Advanced settings" → Secrets** and add:
   ```
   GEMINI_API_KEY = "your_actual_api_key_here"
   ```
5. Click **Deploy**. Your app will be live at `https://<your-app-name>.streamlit.app`.

## 📂 Project Structure
```
app.py             # Streamlit UI (all tabs/pages)
gemini.py          # Gemini API integration
prompts.py         # AI prompt templates
recommendation.py  # Course recommendation engine
database.py        # SQLite persistence layer
pdf_export.py       # PDF roadmap export
requirements.txt   # Python dependencies
.env.example       # Template for your local API key file
```

## 📌 Note
`.env` and the local `data/` folder (SQLite DB) are intentionally excluded via `.gitignore` — never commit API keys or local student data to a public repository.